IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026":
-- PART 10A, TRANSFER OF REGISTRATION: s 359 (registration), lines 23246 to 23333 of CoA1967.txt.
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is the text's yes; JUST FALSE is the text's no in its own words; NOTHING is "the text does not say"
-- (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sge)"). A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- Periods are counted by sg-periods.l4 only (conventions P1 to P9 there, assumed, not ruled): "within 60 days after" opens the day after the event.
-- A trace counts days from AT 0, the day of the event; an act AT n is done n days after it.

DECLARE `s 359 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 359(3) issue a notice of transfer of registration`
    `s 359(4) issue a certificate of confirmation of registration`
    `s 359(6) submit to the Registrar a document evidencing that the foreign corporate entity has been deregistered in its place of incorporation`
    `s 359(9) appeal to the Minister`

§ `Section 359(1): the Registrar may register`

-- "Subject to section 360, upon compliance by the foreign corporate entity with section 358, the Registrar may, if the Registrar thinks fit,
-- register the foreign corporate entity as a company limited by shares by registering its constitution."
-- Three gates, taken in the order the sentence gives them: "Subject to section 360" (a bar; section 360 says "must refuse"),
-- "upon compliance ... with section 358" (an "upon" gate), "if the Registrar thinks fit" (the Registrar's judgment, a conditional input).
-- src:23248 | 359.—(1) Subject to section 360, upon compliance by the foreign
-- src:23249 | corporate entity with section 358, the Registrar may, if the Registrar
-- src:23254 | thinks fit, register the foreign corporate entity as a company limited
-- src:23255 | by shares by registering its constitution.
@ref s 359(1) (src:23248-23255)
GIVEN `section 360 requires the Registrar to refuse to register the foreign corporate entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign corporate entity has complied with section 358` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar thinks fit to register the foreign corporate entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 359(1) the Registrar may register the foreign corporate entity as a company limited by shares` MEANS
    IF `section 360 requires the Registrar to refuse to register the foreign corporate entity`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to section 360 ..." and section 360(1), (2): "The Registrar must refuse to register a foreign corporate entity if ..."
    ELSE (IF NOT `the foreign corporate entity has complied with section 358`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "upon compliance by the foreign corporate entity with section 358" (an "upon" gate on a "may": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (b) and (c); listed as an "upon" site in NOTES.md, Split sites (sge), fork line F-359-8, and for a lawyer)
          ELSE (IF `the Registrar thinks fit to register the foreign corporate entity`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Registrar may, if the Registrar thinks fit, register": a grant whose "if" gate failed (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line F-359-1 in NOTES.md)

§ `Section 359(2): conditions on the registration`

-- "The registration of the foreign corporate entity is subject to such conditions that the Registrar may impose."
-- src:23259 | (2) The registration of the foreign corporate entity is subject to such
-- src:23260 | conditions that the Registrar may impose.
@ref s 359(2) (src:23259-23260)
GIVEN `the Registrar has imposed the condition on the registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 359(2) the registration is subject to the condition` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has imposed the condition on the registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "subject to such conditions that the Registrar may impose" says only that a condition the Registrar imposes binds the registration; it says nothing of a condition the Registrar has not imposed

§ `Section 359(3): the notice of transfer of registration`

-- "Upon registration of the foreign corporate entity, the Registrar must issue a notice of transfer of registration in the prescribed form
-- stating that the company is, on and from the date specified in the notice — (a) registered by way of transfer of registration under this Act;
-- (b) a company limited by shares; and (c) where applicable, a private company."
-- The duty as a regulative rule: "Upon registration" is a trigger, not a time limit, and the text states no consequence, so it has no breach path.
-- src:23264 | (3) Upon registration of the foreign corporate entity, the Registrar
-- src:23265 | must issue a notice of transfer of registration in the prescribed form
-- src:23266 | stating that the company is, on and from the date specified in the
-- src:23267 | notice —
-- src:23269 | (a) registered by way of transfer of registration under this Act;
-- src:23271 | (b) a company limited by shares; and
-- src:23273 | (c) where applicable, a private company.
@ref s 359(3) (src:23264-23273)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 359 act`
`s 359(3) upon registration the Registrar must issue a notice of transfer of registration` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 359(3) issue a notice of transfer of registration`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not issue a notice of transfer of registration upon registration"

-- (a) the notice states that the company is, on and from the date specified, registered by way of transfer of registration under this Act.
-- src:23269 | (a) registered by way of transfer of registration under this Act;
@ref s 359(3)(a) (src:23269-23269)
GIVEN `the notice states that the company is, on and from the date specified in the notice, registered by way of transfer of registration under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 359(3)(a) the notice states that the company is registered by way of transfer of registration` MEANS
    IF `the notice states that the company is, on and from the date specified in the notice, registered by way of transfer of registration under this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Registrar must issue a notice ... stating that the company is ... (a) registered by way of transfer of registration under this Act" (a "must": a notice without the statement does not meet it)

-- (b) the notice states that the company is, on and from the date specified, a company limited by shares.
-- src:23271 | (b) a company limited by shares; and
@ref s 359(3)(b) (src:23271-23271)
GIVEN `the notice states that the company is, on and from the date specified in the notice, a company limited by shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 359(3)(b) the notice states that the company is a company limited by shares` MEANS
    IF `the notice states that the company is, on and from the date specified in the notice, a company limited by shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "stating that the company is ... (b) a company limited by shares"

-- (c) "where applicable, a private company". The text does not say when it is applicable, and s 4(1) "private company" has no limb for a company
-- registered by transfer (finding in NOTES.md), so the company's being a private company is a plain input, and the notice must say so where it is.
-- src:23273 | (c) where applicable, a private company.
@ref s 359(3)(c) (src:23273-23273)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that the company is, on and from the date specified in the notice, a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 359(3)(c) the notice states that the company is a private company where that applies` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a private company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "where applicable, a private company": the text does not say when a company registered by transfer is a private company (fork line F-359-2 in NOTES.md)
    ELSE (IF `the notice states that the company is, on and from the date specified in the notice, a private company`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "stating that the company is ... (c) where applicable, a private company"

-- The whole subsection: a notice in the prescribed form, specifying the date, with (a), (b) and, where it applies, (c).
-- src:23264 | (3) Upon registration of the foreign corporate entity, the Registrar
-- src:23265 | must issue a notice of transfer of registration in the prescribed form
-- src:23266 | stating that the company is, on and from the date specified in the
-- src:23267 | notice —
@ref s 359(3) (src:23264-23267)
GIVEN `the notice is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies the date on and from which the company is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that the company is, on and from the date specified in the notice, registered by way of transfer of registration under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that the company is, on and from the date specified in the notice, a company limited by shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that the company is, on and from the date specified in the notice, a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 359(3) the notice of transfer of registration is as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the notice is in the prescribed form`
      AND `the notice specifies the date on and from which the company is registered`
      AND `s 359(3)(a) the notice states that the company is registered by way of transfer of registration` `the notice states that the company is, on and from the date specified in the notice, registered by way of transfer of registration under this Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `s 359(3)(b) the notice states that the company is a company limited by shares` `the notice states that the company is, on and from the date specified in the notice, a company limited by shares` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND (   (NOT `the company is a private company`)
           OR `s 359(3)(c) the notice states that the company is a private company where that applies` `the company is a private company` `the notice states that the company is, on and from the date specified in the notice, a private company` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Registrar must issue a notice of transfer of registration in the prescribed form stating that the company is, on and from the date specified in the notice — (a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) where applicable, a private company"

§ `Section 359(4): the certificate of confirmation of registration`

-- "A certificate of confirmation of registration must be issued by the Registrar upon the application of the company."
-- A duty with an "upon" gate: before the company applies the Registrar is not required to issue one (JUST FALSE, ruling (b) and (c) of 2026-11-05;
-- fork line F-359-3 in NOTES.md). "the company" is the entity once registered, so for one not yet registered the text says nothing.
-- src:23277 | (4) A certificate of confirmation of registration must be issued by
-- src:23278 | the Registrar upon the application of the company.
@ref s 359(4) (src:23277-23278)
GIVEN `the foreign corporate entity has been registered under section 359(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has applied for a certificate of confirmation of registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 359(4) the Registrar is required to issue a certificate of confirmation of registration` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the foreign corporate entity has been registered under section 359(1)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "upon the application of the company": the company is the registered entity, and the text says nothing of one not yet registered
    ELSE (IF `the company has applied for a certificate of confirmation of registration`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be issued by the Registrar upon the application of the company" (an "upon" gate: no application, no duty to issue)

-- src:23277 | (4) A certificate of confirmation of registration must be issued by
-- src:23278 | the Registrar upon the application of the company.
@ref s 359(4) (src:23277-23278)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 359 act`
`s 359(4) the Registrar must issue a certificate of confirmation of registration upon the application of the company` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 359(4) issue a certificate of confirmation of registration`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not issue a certificate of confirmation of registration upon the application of the company"

§ `Section 359(5): the notice and the certificate are conclusive evidence`

-- "A notice of transfer of registration issued under subsection (3), and a certificate of confirmation of registration issued under
-- subsection (4), is each conclusive evidence — (a) that the foreign corporate entity is registered under this section; and (b) of the date of
-- the company's registration."
-- src:23282 | (5) A notice of transfer of registration issued under subsection (3),
-- src:23283 | and a certificate of confirmation of registration issued under
-- src:23284 | subsection (4), is each conclusive evidence —
-- src:23286 | (a) that the foreign corporate entity is registered under this
-- src:23287 | section; and
@ref s 359(5)(a) (src:23282-23287)
GIVEN `the document is a notice of transfer of registration issued under section 359(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is a certificate of confirmation of registration issued under section 359(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 359(5)(a) the document is conclusive evidence that the foreign corporate entity is registered under section 359` MEANS
    IF `the document is a notice of transfer of registration issued under section 359(3)` OR `the document is a certificate of confirmation of registration issued under section 359(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names two documents and says nothing of any other

-- src:23282 | (5) A notice of transfer of registration issued under subsection (3),
-- src:23283 | and a certificate of confirmation of registration issued under
-- src:23284 | subsection (4), is each conclusive evidence —
-- src:23289 | (b) of the date of the company’s registration.
@ref s 359(5)(b) (src:23282-23289)
GIVEN `the document is a notice of transfer of registration issued under section 359(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is a certificate of confirmation of registration issued under section 359(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the company's registration that the document states` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 359(5)(b) the date of the company's registration that the document conclusively shows` MEANS
    IF `the document is a notice of transfer of registration issued under section 359(3)` OR `the document is a certificate of confirmation of registration issued under section 359(4)`
    THEN JUST `the date of the company's registration that the document states`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names two documents and says nothing of any other

§ `Section 359(6): evidence that the entity has been deregistered in its place of incorporation`

-- "A foreign corporate entity registered under this section must, within 60 days after the issue of the notice of transfer of registration
-- under subsection (3), or such further period as may be extended under subsection (7), submit to the Registrar a document evidencing that the
-- foreign corporate entity has been deregistered in its place of incorporation."
-- The Registrar's extension is given as the last day of the extended period (the text does not say how it is expressed: fork line F-359-4).
-- src:23293 | (6) A foreign corporate entity registered under this section must,
-- src:23294 | within 60 days after the issue of the notice of transfer of registration
-- src:23295 | under subsection (3), or such further period as may be extended under
-- src:23296 | subsection (7), submit to the Registrar a document evidencing that the
-- src:23297 | foreign corporate entity has been deregistered in its place of
-- src:23298 | incorporation.
@ref s 359(6) (src:23293-23298)
GIVEN `the date the notice of transfer of registration was issued` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar has extended the 60-day period under section 359(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the extended period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 359(6) the last day for submitting the document evidencing deregistration` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has extended the 60-day period under section 359(7)`
    THEN `the last day of the extended period`
    ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the notice of transfer of registration was issued` 60 Days

-- src:23293 | (6) A foreign corporate entity registered under this section must,
-- src:23294 | within 60 days after the issue of the notice of transfer of registration
-- src:23295 | under subsection (3), or such further period as may be extended under
-- src:23296 | subsection (7), submit to the Registrar a document evidencing that the
-- src:23297 | foreign corporate entity has been deregistered in its place of
-- src:23298 | incorporation.
@ref s 359(6) (src:23293-23298)
GIVEN `the date the notice of transfer of registration was issued` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar has extended the 60-day period under section 359(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the extended period` IS A DATE
      `the date the document was submitted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 359(6) the day is within the time allowed for submitting the document` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has extended the 60-day period under section 359(7)`
    THEN (`the date the document was submitted` GREATER THAN `the date the notice of transfer of registration was issued`) AND (`the date the document was submitted` AT MOST `the last day of the extended period`)
    ELSE `period: the date is within a period after` `the date the notice of transfer of registration was issued` `the date the document was submitted` 60 Days

-- src:23293 | (6) A foreign corporate entity registered under this section must,
-- src:23294 | within 60 days after the issue of the notice of transfer of registration
-- src:23295 | under subsection (3), or such further period as may be extended under
-- src:23296 | subsection (7), submit to the Registrar a document evidencing that the
-- src:23297 | foreign corporate entity has been deregistered in its place of
-- src:23298 | incorporation.
@ref s 359(6) (src:23293-23298)
GIVEN `the date the notice of transfer of registration was issued` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar has extended the 60-day period under section 359(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the extended period` IS A DATE
      `the foreign corporate entity has submitted to the Registrar a document evidencing that it has been deregistered in its place of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the document was submitted` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 359(6) the foreign corporate entity has complied with the duty to submit the document evidencing deregistration` MEANS
    IF `the foreign corporate entity has submitted to the Registrar a document evidencing that it has been deregistered in its place of incorporation`
    THEN (IF `s 359(6) the day is within the time allowed for submitting the document` `the date the notice of transfer of registration was issued` `the Registrar has extended the 60-day period under section 359(7)` `the last day of the extended period` `the date the document was submitted`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, within 60 days after the issue of the notice ..., or such further period as may be extended under subsection (7), submit" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (a))
    ELSE (IF `the date on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `s 359(6) the last day for submitting the document evidencing deregistration` `the date the notice of transfer of registration was issued` `the Registrar has extended the 60-day period under section 359(7)` `the last day of the extended period`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, within 60 days after the issue of the notice ... submit": the period has run out and no document has been submitted
          ELSE NOTHING)     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period the text states has not yet run out, so the duty is neither met nor missed

-- The duty as a regulative rule. The time limit is the stated period, in days from the issue of the notice (AT 0); `the number of days allowed`
-- is 60, or the length of the period as the Registrar extended it. The consequence the text states (revocation, s 362(1)) is a power of
-- the Registrar, so the LEST is a bare breach.
-- src:23293 | (6) A foreign corporate entity registered under this section must,
-- src:23294 | within 60 days after the issue of the notice of transfer of registration
-- src:23295 | under subsection (3), or such further period as may be extended under
-- src:23296 | subsection (7), submit to the Registrar a document evidencing that the
-- src:23297 | foreign corporate entity has been deregistered in its place of
-- src:23298 | incorporation.
@ref s 359(6) (src:23293-23298)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days allowed for submitting the document` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 359 act`
`s 359(6) the foreign corporate entity registered under this section must submit the document evidencing deregistration` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 359(6) submit to the Registrar a document evidencing that the foreign corporate entity has been deregistered in its place of incorporation`
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed for submitting the document`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the foreign corporate entity did not submit to the Registrar, in time, a document evidencing that it has been deregistered in its place of incorporation"

§ `Section 359(7): the Registrar may extend the 60 days`

-- "The Registrar may, on the application of the foreign corporate entity registered under this section, extend the 60-day period mentioned in
-- subsection (6) subject to such conditions as the Registrar considers fit."
-- "on the application of": the short form of "upon the application of", so an "upon" gate (JUST FALSE without an application: the periods ruling
-- of 2026-11-05, (b) and (c); listed in NOTES.md, Split sites (sge)).
-- src:23302 | (7) The Registrar may, on the application of the foreign corporate
-- src:23303 | entity registered under this section, extend the 60‑day period
-- src:23304 | mentioned in subsection (6) subject to such conditions as the
-- src:23305 | Registrar considers fit.
@ref s 359(7) (src:23302-23305)
GIVEN `the foreign corporate entity is registered under section 359(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign corporate entity has applied for an extension of the 60-day period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 359(7) the Registrar may extend the 60-day period` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the foreign corporate entity is registered under section 359(1)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given "on the application of the foreign corporate entity registered under this section"; for an entity not registered the text says nothing
    ELSE (IF `the foreign corporate entity has applied for an extension of the 60-day period`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar may, on the application of the foreign corporate entity ..., extend" (an "on application" gate, read as "upon": fork line F-359-5 in NOTES.md)

§ `Section 359(8): the Registrar may waive or modify a condition`

-- "The Registrar may, at any time in the Registrar's discretion, waive or modify any condition imposed by the Registrar under subsection (2)."
-- src:23312 | (8) The Registrar may, at any time in the Registrar’s discretion,
-- src:23313 | waive or modify any condition imposed by the Registrar under
-- src:23314 | subsection (2).
@ref s 359(8) (src:23312-23314)
GIVEN `the condition was imposed by the Registrar under section 359(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 359(8) the Registrar may waive or modify the condition` MEANS
    IF `the condition was imposed by the Registrar under section 359(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "any condition imposed by the Registrar under subsection (2)"; for any other condition the text grants nothing and says nothing (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line F-359-6 in NOTES.md)

§ `Section 359(9): appeal to the Minister`

-- "Any person aggrieved by — (a) the refusal of the Registrar to register a foreign corporate entity under subsection (1); (b) any condition of
-- registration imposed by the Registrar under subsection (2); or (c) the modification of any condition by the Registrar under subsection (8),
-- may within 30 days after the date of the refusal to register, or the imposition or modification of the condition (as the case may be),
-- appeal to the Minister whose decision is final."
DECLARE `s 359(9) decision` IS ONE OF
    `s 359(9)(a) the refusal of the Registrar to register a foreign corporate entity under subsection (1)`
    `s 359(9)(b) a condition of registration imposed by the Registrar under subsection (2)`
    `s 359(9)(c) the modification of a condition by the Registrar under subsection (8)`
    `s 359(9) some other decision`

-- src:23318 | (9) Any person aggrieved by —
-- src:23320 | (a) the refusal of the Registrar to register a foreign corporate
-- src:23321 | entity under subsection (1);
-- src:23323 | (b) any condition of registration imposed by the Registrar
-- src:23324 | under subsection (2); or
-- src:23326 | (c) the modification of any condition by the Registrar under
-- src:23327 | subsection (8),
-- src:23329 | may within 30 days after the date of the refusal to register, or the
-- src:23330 | imposition or modification of the condition (as the case may be),
-- src:23331 | appeal to the Minister whose decision is final.
@ref s 359(9) (src:23318-23331)
GIVEN `the person is aggrieved by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision the person is aggrieved by` IS A `s 359(9) decision`
      `the date of the decision` IS A DATE
      `the date the appeal is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 359(9) the person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is aggrieved by the decision`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person aggrieved by" one of the three decisions; for anyone else the text grants nothing and says nothing (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line F-359-7 in NOTES.md)
    ELSE (CONSIDER `the decision the person is aggrieved by`
          WHEN `s 359(9) some other decision` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is given against the refusal, a condition imposed, or the modification of a condition, and no other decision
          OTHERWISE (IF `period: the date is within a period after` `the date of the decision` `the date the appeal is made` 30 Days
                     THEN JUST TRUE
                     ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may within 30 days after the date of the refusal to register, or the imposition or modification of the condition" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (a))

-- src:23329 | may within 30 days after the date of the refusal to register, or the
-- src:23330 | imposition or modification of the condition (as the case may be),
-- src:23331 | appeal to the Minister whose decision is final.
@ref s 359(9) (src:23329-23331)
GIVEN `the decision is the Minister's decision on an appeal under section 359(9)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 359(9) the Minister's decision on the appeal is final` MEANS
    IF `the decision is the Minister's decision on an appeal under section 359(9)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "appeal to the Minister whose decision is final" speaks of the Minister's decision on this appeal only

-- The appeal as a regulative rule: a permission with a stated window of 30 days after the decision (AT 0 is the day of the decision).
-- A permission cannot be breached: an unused one lapses without consequence (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path (sge)").
-- src:23329 | may within 30 days after the date of the refusal to register, or the
-- src:23330 | imposition or modification of the condition (as the case may be),
-- src:23331 | appeal to the Minister whose decision is final.
@ref s 359(9) (src:23329-23331)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 359 act`
`s 359(9) a person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister within 30 days` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    MAY `s 359(9) appeal to the Minister`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
